    "finalText": "Done. The implementation is complete and verified:\n\n- **`POST /links`** — validates absolute http/https URLs with a host, optional 4–20 char codes (`[A-Za-z0-9_-]`), auto-generates unique codes, returns 201 with `clicks: 0`, 409 on duplicate, 422 for malformed/invalid input.\n- **`GET /links/{code}`**, **`GET /links`** (ascending creation order, `items`/`total`), **`GET /r/{code}`** (302 + atomic single increment via one `UPDATE`, JSON 404 for unknown codes).\n- **Persistence** — PostgreSQL via `database/sql` + pgx, `DATABASE_URL` from env, embedded SQL migrations tracked in `schema_migrations`; click counts confirmed to survive restarts, and 8 parallel redirects incremented exactly 8 times.\n- **`sh start.sh`** — builds from vendored deps (offline-safe), applies pending migrations, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; README documents startup.\n\nThe database was reset to a clean state (0 rows) and port 8000 is free, ready for the test suite."
